viewGuide=function(){$('#view').innerHTML='<h2>Guide</h2><p class="subtitle">Obol v2.2 is an offline methodology and reporting assistant. It never executes commands. The maneuver is the unit of methodology; tools are interchangeable implementations.</p><div class="card"><div class="card-body"><h3>Working loop</h3><ol class="guide-list"><li>Choose the active host/domain and ingest evidence.</li><li>Use Path to see evidence-ranked maneuvers and service/workflow depth.</li><li>Open a maneuver. Obol puts its preferred available implementation first, favoring NetExec where it is a strong fit.</li><li>Use semantic toggles, presets, and advanced switches to build the exact command you want.</li><li>If a tool is missing, click <b>I don’t have this tool</b>. Obol records the exception, gives install/official-source help, and promotes the next-best implementation.</li><li>Run the command yourself, preserve evidence, and record only what the output proves.</li><li>Use Report to review the compromise chain and screenshot/evidence readiness before export.</li></ol></div></div><div class="card"><div class="card-body"><h3>v2.2 changes</h3><ul class="guide-list"><li>Maneuvers are separated from tool implementations so alternatives do not distort coverage.</li><li>NetExec is systematically preferred for the protocols/capabilities where it excels, while smbclient, enum4linux-ng, rpcclient and others remain one-click alternatives.</li><li>Command builders now use human-readable intent labels, grouped options, presets, and optional advanced switches.</li><li>Normal Kali availability is assumed; explicit missing-tool choices override that assumption locally.</li><li>Tool help includes copyable install/verify commands and official project links.</li><li>Service depth and workflow progress expose shallow enumeration more precisely.</li><li>Intake recognizes more post-foothold, web, SMB/RPC, sudo/capability, and network evidence while treating tool/transport failures as inconclusive.</li><li>Reports synthesize material compromise transitions separately from routine enumeration and track per-target screenshot/evidence readiness.</li></ul></div></div>';};

