function viewGuide50(){const v=$('#view');if(!v)return;v.innerHTML='<h2>Guide</h2><p class="subtitle">Obol is a human-run workflow: record scope, ingest reviewed Evidence, choose a grounded next step, run commands externally, paste results back, and preserve proof for reporting.</p><div class="card"><div class="card-body"><h3>Core workflow</h3><ol class="guide-list"><li>Define or switch target context in <a href="#/boxes">Targets</a>.</li><li>Paste terminal or tool output into <a href="#/intake">Evidence</a> and review proposed state before applying it.</li><li>Use <a href="#/path">Next Steps</a> for evidence-ranked methodology. Recommendations never execute themselves.</li><li>Open a methodology card, adjust meaningful command controls, copy the command, and run it yourself in the authorized environment.</li><li>Paste the result back into Evidence. Explicit output establishes only the facts supported by that profile.</li><li>Use <a href="#/report">Report</a> to close proof gaps and export a reproducible working draft.</li></ol></div></div><div class="card"><div class="card-body"><h3>Project health and history</h3><p>The <a href="#/dashboard">North Star Dashboard</a> is the single in-app location for project-wide methodology, operator-loop, execution, tool-review, reporting, UI/UX, trend, and backlog metrics. Release history lives in <a href="https://github.com/platocres/obol/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CHANGELOG.md</a>, not in the Guide or README.</p></div></div><div class="card"><div class="card-body"><h3>Evidence and proof boundaries</h3><p>Recognizing a command proves only that an action was attempted. Success requires explicit output appropriate to the workflow. Generated tickets, certificates, relay listeners, startup banners, and discovery text do not silently become access, privilege, or compromise facts.</p></div></div>';syncVersion50();}
